  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing food and nutrition assistance to food insecure people living in the department of Nsanje and Machinga</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to provide moderate acute malnutrition (MAM) treatment in the Machinga district, and food assistance in the Nsanje district, in coordination with the Nutrition and Food Security- Food Assistance clusters. Activities under the Nutrition cluster include distribution of Super Cereal Plus, and nutrition social behavior change communication messaging to raise awareness surrounding nutrition. This will target 6,286 children, aged 6-59 months old. Activities in coordination with the Food Security- Food Assistance cluster will include the procurement and distribution of maize to 55,000 people for one month. This includes 42,778 children, 6,722 women, and 550 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
